      subcategory: 'Web',
      mission: 'Metegrity is the corporate website of a global leader in industrial asset integrity management software, with a presence in over 1,350 facilities across five continents and managed assets exceeding one trillion dollars. The platform protects industrial plants in the chemical, petrochemical, oil & gas, power generation, and pulp & paper sectors. The frontend was built with Astro v6 as the SSG framework, vanilla CSS3 with native variables and Grid/Flexbox layouts, pure JavaScript for IntersectionObserver-driven interactions, and advanced SVG animations with CSS keyframes for industrial diagrams and visualizations. The architecture deliberately avoids Tailwind CSS and component frameworks like React or Vue, prioritizing maximum performance and total code control.',
      problem: '> metegrity@mission-control:~$ diagnostics --run\n\nERROR: A company managing assets valued in the trillions\nof dollars needs a website that conveys technical\nsolidity and industrial reliability at the level\nof its global operation.\n\nWARN: The previous site did not reflect the company\'s\nscale. The experience of complex products (Visions\nEnterprise, RBI, VisionsGo) required clear presentations\nwithout unnecessary jargon.\n\nCRITICAL: Performance had to be flawless for an audience\nof industrial engineers and executives who evaluate\nvendors in seconds. Every SVG diagram had to communicate\ntechnical complexity with elegance.',
